        g = \tanh(W_{ig} x + b_{ig} + W_{hg} h + b_{hg}) \\
        o = \sigma(W_{io} x + b_{io} + W_{ho} h + b_{ho}) \\
        c' = f \odot c + i \odot g \\
        h' = o \odot \tanh(c') \\
        \end{array}

    where :math:`\sigma` is the sigmoid function, and :math:`\odot` is the Hadamard product.

    Args:
